--   Gradient of the linear functional $\langle c, \cdot \rangle$
-- statement:
--   In a real inner product space $E$, the continuous linear functional $z \mapsto \langle c, z\rangle$ attached to a fixed vector $c \in E$ has gradient $c$ at every point:
--   $$\nabla (z \mapsto \langle c, z\rangle)(x) = c \qquad (x \in E).$$
--   This is the elementary case that makes the function $\varphi = f - \langle g_j, \cdot\rangle$ of the smooth-convex interpolation residual differentiable with $\nabla \varphi = \nabla f - g_j$.
